<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador trade suplus falls to $34 mln in April.</title>
<headline>Ecuador trade suplus falls to $34 mln in April.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's trade surplus shrank to $34 million in April from $86 million in the same month of 1996 and $93 million last March, the Central Bank said Thursday.</p>
<p>Exports grew 2.5 percent year-on-year in April to $406 million, while imports surged 20 percent to $372 million.</p>
